  Early Valuation of Genentech

  Genentech was founded in 1976 by entrepreneur Robert Swanson and bio-
  chemist Herbert Boyer to use gene-splicing technology to develop new phar-
  maceuticals. Genentech, devoid of profit, went public in 1980 and raised
  $35 million. With little cash flow in sight, Genentech was valued solely on
  its potential to exploit its intellectual property and introduce important new
  pharmaceuticals. Genentech became profitable in 1993, and was acquired by
  Roche in 2009.


